 " nor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["ParallelMap"]], "paclet:ref/ParallelMap"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->{"InlineFormula"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "9b372fcb-87fb-4ee7-8017-a802c94a32f8"],
 ", and refuses to raise a slot whose vector bundle has no metric."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->817,ExpressionUUID->"858fca7e-d78e-4b35-a70d-16b90a12ee04"],

Cell["\<\
Compute[sol[object, key, $auto, autoKey]] computes the components of autoKey \
by walking the Chain stored under its Routine, and records the result under \
Value so that it survives SaveData.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->818,ExpressionUUID->"d12a2c47-543d-474d-b2ec-00761cfaf840"],

Cell["\<\
Compute[sol[object, key]] does this for every automatic tensor of the entry.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->819,ExpressionUUID->"396e329c-0bc0-42c0-b579-2d4e647a096c"],

Cell["\<\
A Chain entry of the form HoldForm[expr] -> {slots} evaluates expr, with \
$self standing for the solution, and takes it as the components for those \
index slots. An entry of the form {slots} -> {slots} obtains the right-hand \
slots from the left-hand ones by raising or lowering with the metric. In a \
slot specification -1 is a lowered index and 1 a raised one.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->820,ExpressionUUID->"11b7ad70-ecee-45b0-a09b-09823926c9f2"],

Cell["\<\
A raising entry names one slot configuration and fills the whole of its \
ValID, which is the orbit of that configuration under the tensor's signed \
symmetry group. Moving an index past another is a slot permutation and needs \
no metric, so every arrangement reachable that way is given values by the \
same entry, each with the sign its symmetry demands. Raising one slot of \
Riemanncd therefore also resolves the components whose canonical \
representative carries the raised index elsewhere.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->821,ExpressionUUID->"e5712de9-9068-4450-8683-d5b3e4f5abbd"],

Cell["\<\
What a single entry cannot supply is a configuration with a different number \
of raised indices: that one does need the metric, and it gets its own entry. \
This is what a raising ladder is, and it is why a partial chain is legitimate \
-- Compute does exactly what the Chain names, so the user decides which \
levels are computed and when.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->822,ExpressionUUID->"f6eff665-dd5a-4139-a7c1-ca9a9d67668a"],

Cell["\<\
Nothing is computed if the Chain is unset, which is its initial state. \
Compute is silent in that case. The one exception is the companion tensor of \
a differential form, which is given a chain automatically when the form is \
included.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->823,ExpressionUUID->"ee167e32-4fe6-4006-b2e4-97eb5b32cdbe"],

Cell["\<\
Components of a differential form are normally computed with Apply -> {Map -> \
Identity}, since simplifying a wedge product is rarely what is wanted.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->824,ExpressionUUID->"fa3df2c1-1d62-41ce-b06a-d03d9c9d5719"],

Cell["\<\
The option Chain overrides the stored recipe and stores the one given. The \
option Using chooses the metric used for each bundle, and defaults to the \
first metric of that bundle. The option Apply defaults to $Apply.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->825,ExpressionUUID->"857c8687-d0ed-46b4-b3a9-5acbcb6e1bed"],

Cell["\<\
Before computing anything, Compute checks the Chain's slot specification \
against the object: a slot specification of the wrong length, or any slot \
specification at all for a form or a scalar, is reported and nothing is \
computed. It also refuses to raise a slot whose vector bundle has no metric.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->826,ExpressionUUID->"ce174e9c-7d30-4c3a-b312-4a99bb6da310"],

Cell["\<\
Because the recipe is stored beside the answer, a saved solution can always \
be recomputed from scratch rather than merely trusted.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->827,ExpressionUUID->"c1d18447-9343-43f9-984f-7d0ba2f30682"],

Cell["Compute has the attribute HoldFirst.", "Notes",
 CellID->828,ExpressionUUID->"ffbec337-5d01-4f10-bc72-b8d84bf614ae"]
}, Open  ]],

